# A damped pendulum: θ'' = -sin θ - 0.2 θ', let go at 2 radians (about 115
# degrees) from rest. p is the angle, w the angular velocity; F² is the sine.
# The swings shrink and the pendulum turns back through zero each time. t
# drifts: after 160 steps of .05 it is typed .80000123+01, because .05 is not
# exact in binary and each step rounds t + h again.
    t = 0,
    h = 0.05,
    p = 2,
    w = 0,
1   PRINT t, p, w.
    n = 0,
2   Dp = w,
    Dw = -F^2(p) - 0.2w,
    n = n + 1,
    e = n - 9.5,
    CP 2,
    e = t - 9.75,
    CP 1,
    STOP
